<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas hi-pro premiums increase.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas hi-pro premiums increase.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were generally steady on Wednesday although there was an increase in premiums for high protein wheats in some parts of Kansas, dealers said.</p>
<p>They noted that some grain dealers had made contracts with mills in the Kansas City and Topeka areas to sell them high protein wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;They (grain dealers) are scrambling for it now,&quot; a Kansas dealer said of high protein supplies.</p>
<p>Premiums for high protein wheat in Oklahoma and the U.S. Gulf, however, remained unchanged.  </p>
